  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nA circle $C$ of radius 1 is inscribed in an equilateral $\\triangle P Q R$. The points of contact of $C$ with the sides $P Q, Q R, R P$ are $D, E, F$ respectively. The line $P Q$ is given by the equation\n$\\sqrt{3} x+y-6=0$ and the point $D$ is $\\left(\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\frac{3}{2}\\right)$. Further, it is given that the origin and the centre of $C$ are on the same side of the line $P Q$.<strong>Question:</strong>\nEquations of the sides $Q R, R P$ are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wboGj",
      "text": "\n$y=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} x+1, y=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} x-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "snzn6",
      "text": "\n$y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} x, y=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "K1dr5",
      "text": "\n$y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} x+1, y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} x-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Uahjc",
      "text": "\n$y=\\sqrt{3} x, y=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
